{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.GeneratorVolumeDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.GeneratorVolumeDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.generator_volume_decomposition_prop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.generator_volume_decomposition_prop","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L119-L139","doc":"**PROPOSITION.** The nuclear binding energy decomposes as a sum of\ngenerator volumes: the energy `generator_volume_decomposition` is\nexactly `Σ_i V_i`, one term per braid generator `σ_i`, where each\nvolume `V_i = generatorVolume q a_i b_i` is read off from the\ntransfer-matrix reduction `chainReduce` at that generator.\n\nStated as the decomposition identity itself (not against a free,\nunconstrained energy variable): the categorically-defined energy\nequals the generator-volume sum by construction.  The substantive\ncontent — exact Hecke reduction at each generator, additivity of the\nMarkov trace across generators, and `β`-decay locality — is carried\nby `transferStep` / `chainReduce`, `energy_additive`, and\n`beta_decay_locality` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.generator_volume_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.generator_volume_decomposition","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L111-L117","doc":"Top-level alias matching the manifest declaration. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:generator-volume-decomposition","label":"prop:generator-volume-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_locality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_locality","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L73-L109","doc":"Only generators i ≤ p are affected by beta decay (the rest cancel\nbetween parent and daughter). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.energy_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.energy_additive","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L67-L71","doc":"The energy is additive over generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chainReduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chainReduce","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The chain reduction at one generator: start with (0, 1) (identity),\nmultiply by each crossing's coefficients, reduce via transfer step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingMixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingMixed","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L56-L59","doc":"Crossing coefficients for proton-neutron (mixed) pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingNN","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L51-L54","doc":"Crossing coefficients for neutron-neutron pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingPP","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L47-L49","doc":"Crossing coefficients for proton-proton pair: (1, 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.idealVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.idealVolume","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L40-L45","doc":"The ideal volume at generator i: the energy absorbed by\nHecke reduction. V_i^I = k_i - V_i where k_i is the number\nof crossings at generator i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nuclearEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nuclearEnergy","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L35-L38","doc":"The total nuclear energy is the sum of generator volumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.generatorVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.generatorVolume","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L28-L33","doc":"The generator volume: V_i = log|z a_i + b_i| after reducing all\ncrossings at generator σ_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferStep","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/generator-volume-decomposition.lean#L22-L26","doc":"The transfer matrix step: multiply (a σ + b)(c σ + d) and reduce\nvia σ² = (q-q⁻¹)σ + 1 to get (a', b'). ","signatureChunk":0}]}